WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:09.840
To make the most of your pre-consultation and design a look you'll love, it helps to bring these three things.

2
00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:14.664
First, a photo of the hanbok (or outfit) you'll wear on the day.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.496
The color and pattern of the jeogori determine which makeup colors and hair design will suit you best.

4
00:00:20.832 --> 00:00:30.168
If you haven't chosen your hanbok yet, it's best to get a personal color analysis first and find the shade that suits you most before visiting the hanbok shop.

5
00:00:30.504 --> 00:00:34.536
Second, know your current hair condition accurately.

6
00:00:34.872 --> 00:00:44.040
Checking things like hair length, thickness, and thinning at the crown ahead of time lets us plan whether to use a hairpiece and which volume technique will work best.

7
00:00:44.376 --> 00:00:48.648
Third, jot down your usual makeup habits or anything you're self-conscious about.

8
00:00:48.984 --> 00:00:56.904
Even small concerns, like "Will I need to wear glasses" or "I cry easily and worry about smudging," make a big difference to the final result once you share them with the artist.

9
00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:06.048
Finally, let us know the wedding venue (hotel, church, outdoors, etc.), and we'll suggest a skin finish optimized for that lighting.
